    <description>ReelGeek turns a folder of photographs into a vertical video edit on your own machine.
It builds a real edit rather than a slideshow, and nothing is uploaded anywhere.

* Cuts the shots against a tempo grid instead of fading on a timer
* Gives every shot its own camera move and picks a transition to get out of it
* Renders 1080x1920 H.264 MP4, ready to upload to TikTok or YouTube Shorts
* Reads from disk and renders on the processor, so no graphics card is needed
* No account, no watermark, no export limit

Open source under GPL-3.0. Python and ffmpeg are inside the installer, so there is nothing to
install first.</description>
    <summary>Free offline photo to vertical video maker for Windows, cut to a beat grid</summary>
